[B]ROM:[/B] CyanogenMod 7
[B]Device:[/B] Huawei Y210
[B]Android version:[/B] 2.3.7 Gingerbread
[B]Status:[/B] Status: Beta / mostly usable
[B]Build:[/B] cm-7-20260619-UNOFFICIAL-y210.zip
[B]MD5:[/B] 09b4564ac74dfc5d5546c0f2b1d031b8

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 7 port for the Huawei Y210, based on the legacy Qualcomm MSM7x27A/MSM7K-era stack. The current focus is real device stability and compatibility with the stock Y210 behaviour, especially graphics, gralloc/copybit/framebuffer, audio, radio, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and camera bring-up.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Read before flashing:[/B][/COLOR] this is still a beta release. Please read the known issues before flashing.

[SIZE="4"][B]What works:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Boot & system:[/B] boots to launcher after a clean flash/wipe
[*][B]SurfaceFlinger / mediaserver:[/B] stay alive in the current graphics path
[*][B]Display / framebuffer:[/B] gralloc.y210 and copybit.y210 load without crashing the UI; 320x480 ARGB8888 framebuffer
[*][B]HW acceleration:[/B] Adreno 200 path active; SurfaceFlinger reports Adreno renderer; stride bug corrected (no horizontal repetition)
[*][B]UI / launcher:[/B] usable on-device; status bar renders correctly (ghost/duplication fixed)
[*][B]Touchscreen:[/B] single-touch and multitouch input; physical and capacitive buttons
[*][B]Backlight / LED / vibrator:[/B] screen backlight, notification LED and vibrator work
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] enables, scans, associates and obtains DHCP; hotspot/tethering validated with two clients
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] enables through the restored QCOM path
[*][B]Telephony / RIL:[/B] baseband, operator registration, signal, IMEI, calls, SMS and HSPA mobile data
[*][B]Sensors / rotation:[/B] accelerometer, gravity and linear-accel sensors work with stock sensors.default.so; /dev/accel permissions corrected
[*][B]ADB / logs:[/B] adb logcat and runtime logging are usable
[*][B]Audio playback:[/B] AudioFlinger -> libaudio output works
[*][B]Audio recording:[/B] SoundRecorder / voice recorder works
[*][B]Camera app:[/B] opens consistently with the current libcamera wrapper
[*][B]Camera:[/B] 640x480 colour portrait preview, JPEG photo capture (~55 KB), close -> reopen, photo/video switch, H.263 352x288 15 fps video recording (MP4 in gallery)
[*][B]Video playback:[/B] compatible files play; H.264 Baseline was tested
[*][B]Storage / USB:[/B] /data, SD card and USB mass storage
[*][B]Suspend / screen off:[/B] screen off/on cycle validated
[*][B]Performance profile:[/B] Y210 CPU governor and lowmemorykiller profile applied at runtime
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Headset audio:[/B] works, but perceived volume is lower than stock (stock uses proprietary DSP processing not available in CM7)
[*][B]Headset volume keys:[/B] vol+ / vol- are acknowledged by the UI but behaviour after headset reconnect still needs validation
[*][B]Voice call uplink:[/B] calls work, but microphone/uplink still needs more real-world validation
[*][B]Bluetooth audio:[/B] pairing and A2DP/SCO audio are still pending validation
[*][B]FM radio:[/B] kernel driver patched to prevent firmware reset on second open; audio output in earphones pending final validation on device
[*][B]Deep sleep / battery drain:[/B] the suspend path sometimes fails (rpcrouter_smd_xprt wakelock); battery may drain faster than expected and deep sleep is not fully confirmed
[*][B]GPS:[/B] RPC/XTRA/NTP/AGPS initialise, but real satellite fix still needs outdoor testing
[*][B]Wi-Fi clean flash:[/B] basic Wi-Fi works, but post-flash validation without manual staging should be repeated
[*][B]Video playback:[/B] compatible H.264 Baseline files play, but newer MP4 files such as H.264 High profile may fail
[*][B]First boot warning:[/B] com.android.provision may log a non-blocking WindowManager InflateException while creating the starting window after wipe
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Changelog:[/B][/SIZE]

[B]2026-06-13[/B]
[LIST]
[*]FM radio: patched tavarua kernel driver to skip hardware re-init when firmware is already loaded, preventing firmware loss on second open of /dev/radio0; audio validation pending
[/LIST]

[B]2026-06-12[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Clean flash validated: first boot completes, PackageManager rebuilds state, launcher starts
[*]Graphics path stable enough for launcher use; gralloc.y210/copybit.y210 no longer collapse the UI
[*]Adreno 200 renderer active in SurfaceFlinger
[*]Wi-Fi validated: enable, scan, associate, DHCP
[*]Bluetooth enables through restored QCOM route
[*]Audio playback and audio recording validated
[*]Camera app opens consistently; 640x480 preview remains stable on first open; video recording validated (H.263 352x288 15 fps → MP4)
[*]Y210 CPU governor and lowmemorykiller runtime profile restored
[*]Accelerometer /dev/accel permissions corrected (chmod 0664 in init.y210.rc was missing indentation and being silently ignored)
[/LIST]

[B]2026-05-24[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed Adreno 200 horizontal stride bug: gralloc forced to single-buffer so EGL receives a PMEM fd instead of the framebuffer fd, giving correct 320 px stride (was 128 px, causing 2.5x image repetition)
[*]Fixed framebuffer copy path to use memcpy instead of MSMFB_BLIT for PMEM sub-heap fds
[*]Fixed FD_CLOEXEC on all persistent audio file descriptors to prevent EBUSY on /dev/msm_pcm_out after fork
[*]Reverted headset post-processing mask from "full" to "lite" (EQ+IIR, no MBADRC) — MBADRC was compressing the DSP output and nullifying the software volume control
[*]Fixed missing keymap: default_keypad.kcm and all keylayout .kl files added to device tree
[*]Fixed ringtone/notification props to use files that exist in CM7 (Huawei_Tune.ogg / Glory.ogg do not exist)
[*]Added HSDPA/HSPA TCP buffer sizes to init.y210.rc
[/LIST]

[B]2026-05-23[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed gralloc.msm7k.so contamination: clean rebuild of libgralloc-qsd8k with Android.mk guards; previous binary had symbols from both gralloc modules causing a bootloop
[/LIST]

[B]2026-05-22[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed status bar ghost/duplication: StatusBarManagerService now skips redundant propagation to mBar when icon state did not change
[*]Fixed RIL double-poll: removed redundant notifyRegistrants() call on events 1033/1037 (DATA_NETWORK_STATE_CHANGED), which was causing rapid signal icon flicker
[*]Fixed page-flip detection in gralloc framebuffer: yres_virtual check corrected; refresh rate guard changed from == 0 to < 1 Hz to correctly detect the Y210 pixel clock
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Hardware notes:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]SoC family: Qualcomm MSM7x27A / MSM7K-era
[*]GPU: Adreno 200
[*]Framebuffer: 320x480, ARGB8888 (32 bpp)
[*]Android base: Gingerbread / CyanogenMod 7
[*]HAL style: legacy Qualcomm/Android 2.3 stack
[*]FM chip: WCN2243 (I2S digital output to MSM7x27A codec)
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Make a full nandroid backup from recovery.
[*]Wipe data / factory reset.
[*]Wipe cache and dalvik cache.
[*]Flash the ROM zip from recovery.
[*]Reboot.
[*]First boot can take a while while PackageManager rebuilds state and dexopts apps.
[/LIST]

[B]Update from a previous build:[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Wipe cache and dalvik cache.
[*]Flash the new build.
[*]Reboot.
[/LIST]

